# sentence_id = 78
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = She also taught me that the abundance which fortune supplies to those who possess the means for an easy life is something to use without vanity and yet without hesitation, so that when such things are present one handles them naturally and unaffectedly, and when they are absent one has no need of them—spending unstintingly on such things.
# literal_translation = And this too: the [thing] which fortune furnishes to those bringing [something] toward easiness of life, of which things fortune supplied abundance: [I learned]: to be a disposition apt-to-use [it], at once without vanity and without hesitation, so-that, while [such things] are present, to touch [them] unaffectedly, and, while [they] are absent, not to be in need [of them].
