# sentence_id = 83
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Above all, I learned the readiness to yield without envy to those who possess some special ability, such as skill in expression, or knowledge derived from the study of law, of custom, or of other matters, and to join eagerly in promoting them, so that each of these men might win esteem according to his own particular merits.
# literal_translation = Especially however: the yielding-without-envy to-those-possessing some ability, such-as the expressive [ability] or that from-study of-laws or of-customs or of-other certain matters, and [I learned] the being-eager-along-with-them, in-order-that each [of them] according to their own merits might-be-well-esteemed.
