# sentence_id = 102
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Not to be subjected to a ruler and a father who was bound to strip away all my vanity and to bring me to the realization that it is possible to live in a court without needing a bodyguard, or elaborate robes, lamps, statues, and the like display, but that it is possible for one to reduce oneself very nearly to the condition of a private citizen, without thereby becoming meaner or more remiss in the duties which a ruler must perform for the common good with authority befitting his office.
# literal_translation = To be subjected to a ruler and to a father: who was about to strip away all the vanity of me, and to bring [me] into the realization that it is possible, while living in a court, not to need bodyguards, nor conspicuous garments, nor such lamps and statues and the like ostentation, but it is permitted to contract oneself very nearly to a private citizen, and not on this account to hold oneself more lowly or more remiss with a view to the things which must be done, on behalf of the common interests, in a manner befitting a leader.
