# sentence_id = 108
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = I learned to form a vivid and frequent picture of what a life lived according to nature is like, so that, as far as depends on the gods and on the communications, dispensations, and inspirations that come from them, nothing should any longer prevent me from living in accordance with nature; and I learned that I fell short of this still, through my own fault and through not heeding the reminders—almost the very instructions—coming from the gods.
# literal_translation = The to-be-imagined concerning the according-to-nature of-life clearly and often: such as someone is, so that, as-much-as depends on the gods and on the from-there dispensations and cooperations and inspirations, nothing to-hinder me from-now living according to nature; and to-fall-short still of-this through my own fault and through the not diligently-keeping the from-the-gods remindings and almost teachings:
